{"availability":"available","full":"sebastian-hanisch/hdbscan-demo","name":"hdbscan-demo","description":"HDBSCAN: die Kombination, die Dichte-Unterschiede UND Chaining entschärft – Sehen Sie, wie HDBSCAN eine dichte-angepasste Distanz mit einer Fusionshierarchie kombiniert und daraus per Kondensierung stabile Cluster gewinnt. Interaktive Streamlit-Demo, Teil von sebastianhanisch.net","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-05T09:19:53Z","updated":"2026-10-04T13:21:51Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sebastianhanisch-hdbscan-demo.streamlit.app/","topics":["clustering","demo","german","machine-learning","python","streamlit"],"demo":"https://sebastianhanisch-hdbscan-demo.streamlit.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:00:51.020Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T19:00:51.020Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T19:00:51.020Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.107Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T09:23:24.733Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T19:00:51.020Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fünftes Stück der \"Konzepte\"-Reihe für die Website \"Sebastian Hanisch – Operations Research und Machine Learning\" - der Zusammenfluss der Clustering-Linie:","HDBSCAN kombiniert genau die zwei Zutaten, die es im Namen trägt: eine hierarchische Fusionsstruktur (wie in agglomerative-demo), angewendet auf eine dichte-angepasste Distanz (den DBSCAN-Kerngedanken aus dbscan-demo) statt der rohen euklidischen Distanz. Zwei der vier Presets recyceln exakt die Härtefall-Szenarien, an denen die beiden Vorläufer nachweislich scheiterten, und zeigen live, dass HDBSCAN beide löst - der Zusammenfluss wird nicht nur behauptet, sondern konkret nachvollziehbar gemacht.","Anders als die Fall-Demos im Portfolio (ein Anwendungsfall, mehrere Verfahren im Vergleich) zeigt diese Demo ein Verfahren – HDBSCAN selbst, nicht eine vierte Methode neben k-Means/DBSCAN/agglomerativem Clustering. Vehikel-Problem: Lieferadressen zu Sammel-Routen gruppieren, ohne eps festlegen zu müssen UND ohne Chaining-Risiko."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/hdbscan-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"acc4218b51b9b9964fa8a42784a8038abe5c190e19db1d8cc3103f8dceb935c9","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.243Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.243Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Fünftes Stück der \"Konzepte\"-Reihe für die Website \"Sebastian Hanisch – Operations Research und Machine Learning\" - der Zusammenfluss der Clustering-Linie:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/hdbscan-demo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"acc4218b51b9b9964fa8a42784a8038abe5c190e19db1d8cc3103f8dceb935c9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/hdbscan-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.243Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T13:21:51Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sebastian-hanisch/hdbscan-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T06:45:35.244Z","hash":"acc4218b51b9b9964fa8a42784a8038abe5c190e19db1d8cc3103f8dceb935c9","originalBytes":8458,"storedBytes":8458,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["die","der","und","hdbscan","cluster","eine","demo","als","auf","den","mit","zwei","aber","baum","cke","agglomerative-demo","beiden","clustering","mehrere","mutual-reachability-distanz","nicht","punkte","soft","venv","aus","diese","ein","fall","kreuzvergleich","ohne","presets","punkt","single-linkage","von","wie","bei","beide","ber","dass","dbscan-demo","dem","dichte","direkt","distanz","erreicht","exakt","gegen","harte","hier","ist","k-means","kein","keine","kern-distanz","nur","rand-index","reihe","selbst","tests","werden","activate","anders","angewendet","app.py","auch","ausf","bash","bereinstimmung","das","dbscan","denen","deutlich","dichte-ungleichgewicht","dies